wcristalle@hotmail.com wrote:
> 
> Why not just add a new food item (or tool) to the game: a lump of salt?
> 
Treat it as a mineral when polymorphing.

> - As suggested, you could (a)pply it to corpses to preserve them
> indefinitely.

A preserved cockatrice corpse would be too powerful. Instead, salting
the corpse could just reset its age to zero, and use up the salt.
Pickling corpses, i.e dipping them in acid, could have the same effect.

> - It would have a much greater chance of being found in the Mines. As
> well, there could be an special, rarely-occurring room (like a treasure
> zoo) containing big lumps of salt hanging from the ceiling: "You enter
> a salt cave!" Of course, among the salt would be various glass
> piercers, disguised as stalactites, waiting to drop on your
> unsuspecting head.

Make them salt piercers. They can do extra damage by rubbing salt
in the wound, and they're only generated in salt caves.

Throwing salt at wounded monsters also does extra damage, by
getting salt in the wounds. Throwing salt into water hurts any
aquatic monster in that square, since they're all fresh water
creatures.

> - Applying it to a potion of water would turn it into salt water -
> though I'm not sure what further effect this would have.

Causes hallucination but cures sickness, both exaggerations of
real-world effects.


